From: Balamurugan Mahalingam <bmahalin@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 30 May 2025 22:20:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: map REO destination to the PPE ring

RxOLE marks direct-switch frames with REO destination index 6, but the
QCN9274 REO destination map must also translate that index to hardware
ring 11.  The QSDK driver installs this mapping from its REO setup path.
Without it, an authorized peer is redirected away from the normal host
ring without reliably reaching REO2PPE, which also loses DHCP traffic.

Install the missing mapping when the direct-switch rings are configured.
Read the register back both to flush the write and to make the effective
configuration visible in the node registration log.

Based-on: 4590caf67ab7de99e7a1ea2bc70d2429b5f855e1
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0337-01-QSDK-DP-wifi-Add-support-for-PPE-DS-Direct-switch-fe.patch
Signed-off-by: Pradeep Kumar Chitrapu <pradeepc@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Balamurugan Mahalingam <bmahalin@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Ramanathan Choodamani <rchoodam@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Ganesh Kariganuru Mahabalesh <gkarigan@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Nithyanantham Paramasivam <nithp@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Nandha Kishore Easwaran <nandhaki@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Pavankumar Nandeshwar <pnandesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Neha Bisht <nbisht@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Aloka Dixit <alokad@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Sidhanta Sahu <sidhanta@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -39,6 +39,9 @@
 
 #define ATH12K_PPE_REO_DEST_REG		(HAL_SEQ_WCSS_UMAC_REO_REG + 0xcf0)
 #define ATH12K_PPE_REO_DEST_VALUE	0x2000
+#define ATH12K_PPE_REO_RING_MAP_REG	(HAL_SEQ_WCSS_UMAC_REO_REG + 0x4)
+#define ATH12K_PPE_REO_RING6_MAP	GENMASK(27, 24)
+#define ATH12K_PPE_REO2PPE_RING_MAP	11
 #define ATH12K_PPE_TCL_RBM_MAP_REG	(HAL_SEQ_WCSS_UMAC_TCL_REG + 0x88)
 #define ATH12K_PPE_TCL_RBM_SHIFT	(7 * 4)
 #define ATH12K_PPE_TCL_RBM_MASK		GENMASK(31, 28)
@@ -600,8 +603,15 @@ static void ath12k_ppe_ds_hw_config(stru
 
 	ath12k_hif_write32(ab, ATH12K_PPE_REO_DEST_REG,
 			   ATH12K_PPE_REO_DEST_VALUE);
+	val = ath12k_hif_read32(ab, ATH12K_PPE_REO_RING_MAP_REG);
+	val &= ~ATH12K_PPE_REO_RING6_MAP;
+	val |= u32_encode_bits(ATH12K_PPE_REO2PPE_RING_MAP,
+			       ATH12K_PPE_REO_RING6_MAP);
+	ath12k_hif_write32(ab, ATH12K_PPE_REO_RING_MAP_REG, val);
+	val = ath12k_hif_read32(ab, ATH12K_PPE_REO_RING_MAP_REG);
+	ath12k_info(ab, "PPE REO ring map configured: 0x%x\n", val);
 	val = ath12k_hif_read32(ab, ATH12K_PPE_TCL_RBM_MAP_REG);
 	val &= ~ATH12K_PPE_TCL_RBM_MASK;
 	val |= HAL_WBM2SW_PPEDS_TX_CMPL_MAP_ID << ATH12K_PPE_TCL_RBM_SHIFT;
 	ath12k_hif_write32(ab, ATH12K_PPE_TCL_RBM_MAP_REG, val);
 }
